hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22281","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Said ibn Sad ibn Ubada, he said: Among our houses was a deformed, weak man. The people of the house expected nothing except he was upon a slave girl of the house committing indecency with her, and he was a Muslim. Sad raised his matter to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Strike him his hadd. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he is weaker than that; if we strike him a hundred, we will kill him. He said: So take for him a palm branch with a hundred stalks and strike him with it one blow, and release him."
